**Causal limits (explicit):** this is a *feature-gap closure* (enhancement issue), not a regression bug; the brief's "issue or failure" wording covers it, but I label it honestly. I verified merge metadata and a code-path commit, but I did **not** open the PR diff commit-by-commit nor run the upstream tests, so "the merge made 1.1.0 support complete" is supported only at the level of milestone+docs concordance, and MP3 availability still depends on the build including mpg123/LAME (PR body). Also note PR body lists WAV-embedded MPEG as *future* work — so "MP3-in-WAV works" must not be claimed.
**Design consequence (inference):** for lossy imports the proposal must define provenance against the *decoded PCM at import time* (e.g., fingerprint of the decoded frames), because the compressed stream, its decoder, and the samples are three different things; the brief's "a numerical time calculation is not evidence the audio content was assembled correctly" applies with full force to lossy sources.

