- **C2.** Do not claim "libsndfile supports RF64 / >4 GB WAV" from the captured formats page — RF64 does not appear there. A two-hour 48 kHz/24-bit stereo mix ≈ 2.1 GB fits WAV's classic 4 GiB field envelope, but the boundary claim needs the actual format/API doc (lead L4). Arithmetic about file size is not evidence of format support — same discipline the brief demands for audio content.
- **C3.** Do not claim "MP3 import is sample-exact" or cite MP3 seeking guarantees beyond the PR body's status list (F4). Lossy decode ⇒ provenance anchors to decoded PCM.
- **C4.** Do not cite Audacity `.aup3`/SQLite, autosave, or dependency-tracking as fact without a fresh fetch (F8). If the final proposal wants those lessons, fetch the doc/source first; otherwise present the analogous design (sidecar manifest + atomic save + import fingerprinting) as this project's own choice.
